   "title": "Statistics Confusable Terms",
   "text": "learning course). normal: the normal distribution is the bell curve. It does not mean \"typical\" or \"healthy\" values.  standardization: in this course standardization means converting values to z-scores with mean 0 and standard deviation 1. adjusted R squared: adjusted R2 = 1 - (1 - R2) * (n - 1) / (n - p - 1) where p is the number of predictors. Plain R2 never decreases when a predictor is added to the model, so adjusted R2 is used to compare models of different sizes. sample: in statistics a sample is a subset drawn from a population. In machine learning courses a sample often means a single row of data.",
